<h1>Hibiki cable spike — counter (ERB)</h1>

<div data-controller="counter" data-counter-cid-value="<%= @cid %>">
  <%= turbo_stream_from "counter", @cid %>

  <%# Paint-avoidance placeholders only: the controller subscribes AFTER the
      Turbo stream confirms (the packaged ChannelController awaits the
      stream source above), so the graph's first broadcast always lands and
      replaces these. They no longer have to match the graph's initial
      state. %>
  <%= render "count", count: 0, doubled: 0 %>
  <%= render "step", step: 1 %>

  <%# The reactive-value shape on the subclass/Turbo-broadcast page: the
      count/step fragments above ride Turbo broadcasts, but reactive +
      transmit_value always use CounterChannel's own subscription, whose
      value messages the ChannelController base's received() writes into
      every matching placeholder — so a single value composes with the
      broadcast transport, no extra controller. Second site below,
      outside this controller element. %>
  <p>doubled (reactive value): <%= reactive :doubled, 0 %></p>

  <p>
    <button data-action="counter#increment">+ step</button>
    <button data-action="counter#burst">burst (10 writes, 1 broadcast)</button>
    <label>
      step:
      <input type="number" value="1" min="1" data-action="change->counter#setStep">
    </label>
  </p>
</div>

<%# The same `doubled` value OUTSIDE the controller element: reactive
    values match document-wide, so this site updates from the same
    transmit_value message as the one inside the island. %>
<p>doubled again (outside the island): <%= reactive :doubled, 0, tag_name: :strong %></p>

<p><a href="/phlex">Phlex stage &rarr;</a> &middot; <a href="/phlex-counter">Phlex counter &rarr;</a></p>

<%# Fragment root ids are the replacement keys (Turbo target here, the
    packaged client's getElementById on the island below) — they must be
    page-unique, which is why the Phlex island's fragments carry
    phlex-prefixed ids next to this page's count/step. %>
<%= render CounterPhlex::Show.new(cid: SecureRandom.uuid) %>